2 > the procedure ends;  
Upon L2 U2N Relay UE receives RRCReject, it either triggers PC5-S release or sends Notification message to the connected L2 U2N Remote UE(s) in accordance with 5.8.9.10.  
The RRC_INACTIVE UE shall continue to monitor paging while the timer T302 is running.

The UE applies the **timeAlignmentTimerCommon** included in SIB1 after triggering an SI request.

Relevant text from context [1] and [2]:
> 2 > apply the timeAlignmentTimerCommon included in SIB1;

The UE shall:  
2 &gt; if event(s) associated to all measId(s) within condTriggerConfig for a target candidate cell within the stored condRRCReconfig are fulfilled:  
3 &gt; consider the target candidate cell within the stored condRRCReconfig, associated to that condReconfigId, as a triggered cell;  
3 &gt; initiate the conditional reconfiguration execution, as specified in 5.3.5.13.5;

Upon receiving a PUCCH release request from lower layers, for all bandwidth parts of an indicated serving cell the UE shall:  
- release PUCCH-CSI-Resources configured in CSI-ReportConfig;  
- release SchedulingRequestResourceConfig instances configured in PUCCH-Config.

The UE re-establishes the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322.

From [3] Clause 5.3.5.5.4 — RLC bearer addition/modification:  
"1 > if the UE's current configuration contains an RLC bearer with the received logicalChannelIdentity/LogicalChannelIdentityExt within the same cell group:  
2 > if the RLC bearer is associated with an DAPS bearer, or  
2 > if any DAPS bearer is configured and the RLC bearer is associated with an SRB:  
3 > reconfigure the RLC entity or entities for the target cell group in accordance with the received rlc-Config;  
3 > reconfigure the logical channel for the target cell group in accordance with the received mac- LogicalChannelConfig;  
3 > if reestablishRLC is received:  
4 > re-establish the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322 ;  
3 > reconfigure the RLC entity or entities in accordance with the received rlc-Config;  
3 > reconfigure the logical channel in accordance with the received mac- LogicalChannelConfig;"

Upon initiating the procedure, the UE shall: 1 > initiate transmission of the FailureInformation message as specified in 5.7.5.3;  

and  

A UE initiates the procedure when there is a need inform the network about a failure detected by the UE. In particular, the UE initiates the procedure when the following condition is met: 1 > upon detecting failure for an RLC bearer, in accordance with 5.3.10.3;

The UE shall:  
2 &gt; if the UE has connection establishment failure information or connection resume failure information available in VarConnEstFailReportList and if the RPLMN is not equal to plmn-identity stored in VarConnEstFailReportList:  
3 &gt; clear the content included in VarConnEstFailReportList;

If a UE in RRC_INACTIVE has joined one or more MBS session(s) indicated by the TMGI included in the pagingGroupList and none of the ue-Identity included in any of the PagingRecord, if included in the Paging message, matches the UE identity allocated by upper layers, the UE shall:

> initiate the RRC connection resumption procedure according to 5.3.13 with resumeCause set as below:  
> if the UE is configured by upper layers with Access Identity 1:  
>> resumeCause is set to mps-PriorityAccess;  
> else if the UE is configured by upper layers with Access Identity 2:  
>> resumeCause is set to mcs-PriorityAccess;  
> else if the UE is configured by upper layers with one or more Access Identities equal to 11-15:  
>> resumeCause is set to highPriorityAccess;  
> otherwise,  
>> resumeCause is set to mt-Access.

The UE shall:  
2 > if an FR1 measurement gap sharing configuration configured by gapSharingFR1 is already setup:  
3 > release the FR1 measurement gap sharing configuration configured by gapSharingFR1;  
2 > setup the FR1 measurement gap sharing configuration indicated by the measGapSharingConfig in accordance with the received gapSharingFR1 as defined in TS 38.133;

The UE shall:  
2 &gt; stop T390 for all access categories;  
2 &gt; perform the actions as specified in 5.3.14.4.

The UE shall:  
2 &gt; stop T390 for all access categories;  
2 &gt; perform the actions as specified in 5.3.14.4.

The UE shall:  
1 > if SCG MAC is not part of the current UE configuration (i.e. SCG establishment):  
2 > create an SCG MAC entity;

The L2 U2N Relay UE shall:  
- re-establish the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322;  
- reconfigure the RLC entity in accordance with the received rlc-Config;  
- reconfigure the logical channel in accordance with the received mac-LogicalChannelConfig.  

(Source: Clause 5.3.5.5.13 — Uu Relay RLC channel addition/modification)

The UE shall:  
1 &gt; if the RRCReestablishment message includes the sl-L2RemoteUEConfig (i.e. the UE is a L2 U2N Remote UE):  
2 &gt; perform the L2 U2N Remote UE configuration procedure as specified in 5.3.5.16;  
2 &gt; consider the current cell to be the PCell;

The L2 U2N Remote UE in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE shall:  
1 > if the UE has not stored a valid version of a SIB, in accordance with clause 5.2.2.2.1, of one or several required SIB(s) in accordance with clause 5.2.2.1:  
2 > include sl-Requested-SI-List in the RemoteUEInformationSidelink to indicate the requested SIB(s);

The L2 U2N Remote UE shall:  
1 &gt; set the sl-Requested-SI-List to the value release;  
1 &gt; set the sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE to the value release;  
1 &gt; submit the RemoteUEInformationSidelink message to lower layers for transmission;

The purpose of the SidelinkUEInformationNR procedure regarding transmission resource management is to:

- **request assignment or release of transmission resource for NR sidelink communication**;
- **indicate the NR sidelink communication transmission resources required by the UE**;
- **indicate it no longer requires NR sidelink communication transmission resources**;
- **request (configuration/release) of NR sidelink discovery announcements transmission resources**;
- **request (configuration/release) of NR sidelink U2N relay communication transmission resources**.

(Source: Clause 5.8.3.1 and Clause 5.8.3.3)

For each sl-ReportConfigId included in the received sl-ReportConfigToRemoveList that is part of the current UE configuration in VarMeasConfigSL, the UE shall:

- remove the entry with the matching sl-ReportConfigId from the sl-ReportConfigList within the VarMeasConfigSL;
- remove all sl-MeasId associated with the sl-ReportConfigId from the sl-MeasIdList within the VarMeasConfigSL, if any;
- if a sl-MeasId is removed from the sl-MeasIdList:
  - remove the measurement reporting entry for this sl-MeasId from the VarMeasReportListSL, if included;
  - stop the periodical reporting timer and reset the associated information (e.g. sl-TimeToTrigger) for this sl-MeasId.

The UE shall:  
2 > remove all sl-MeasId associated with the sl-ReportConfigId from the sl-MeasIdList within the VarMeasConfigSL, if any;  
2 > if a sl-MeasId is removed from the sl-MeasIdList:  
3 > remove the measurement reporting entry for this sl-MeasId from the VarMeasReportListSL, if included;  
3 > stop the periodical reporting timer and reset the associated information (e.g. sl-TimeToTrigger) for this sl-MeasId.

The UE shall:  
1 &gt; if the resumption of the RRC connection is triggered by response to NG-RAN paging:  
2 &gt; select '0' as the Access Category;  
2 &gt; perform the unified access control procedure as specified in 5.3.14 using the selected Access Category and one or more Access Identities provided by upper layers;  
3 &gt; if the access attempt is barred, the procedure ends;

When conditions for initiating SDT in accordance with 5.3.13.1b are fulfilled, the UE:

- considers the resume procedure is initiated for SDT;  
- starts timer T319a;  
- starts timer T319;  
- instructs the MAC entity to consider the cg-SDT-TimeAlignmentTimer as expired, if it is running.  

(From [2] Clause 5.3.13.2 — Initiation: “1 > if conditions for initiating SDT in accordance with 5.3.13.1b are fulfilled: 2 > consider the resume procedure is initiated for SDT; 2 > start timer T319a; 2 > start timer T319; 2 > instruct the MAC entity to consider the cg-SDT-TimeAlignmentTimer as expired, if it is running;”)

The UE shall:  
1 &gt; if the received sl-MeasConfig includes the sl-ReportConfigToAddModList in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink:  
2 &gt; perform the sidelink reporting configuration addition/modification procedure as specified in 5.8.10.2.7;

Upon receiving the SIB8 the UE shall:  
1 > if the SIB8 contains a complete warning message and the complete geographical area coordinates (if any):  
2 > forward the received warning message, messageIdentifier, serialNumber, dataCodingScheme and the geographical area coordinates (if any) to upper layers;  
2 > continue reception of SIB8;  

...and later, for the case where all segments have been received:  
4 > forward the received warning message, messageIdentifier, serialNumber, dataCodingScheme and geographical area coordinates (if any) to upper layers;  
4 > stop assembling a warning message and geographical area coordinates (if any) for this messageIdentifier and serialNumber and delete all stored information held for it;  
3 > continue reception of SIB8;  

Thus, the action the UE takes **after forwarding a complete warning message to upper layers** is:  
**"stop assembling a warning message and geographical area coordinates (if any) for this messageIdentifier and serialNumber and delete all stored information held for it;"**  

This is directly copied from clause [1], subclause "4 >" under the condition "if all segments of a warning message and geographical area coordinates (if any) have been received".

If T304 of the MCG expires and any DAPS bearer is configured without radio link failure detected in the source PCell, the UE shall:

- release dedicated preambles provided in rach-ConfigDedicated if configured;
- release dedicated msgA PUSCH resources provided in rach-ConfigDedicated if configured;
- if any DAPS bearer is configured, and radio link failure is not detected in the source PCell, according to clause 5.3.10.3:
  - reset MAC for the target PCell and release the MAC configuration for the target PCell;
  - for each DAPS bearer:
    - release the RLC entity or entities as specified in TS 38.322 , clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the target PCell;
    - reconfigure the PDCP entity to release DAPS as specified in TS 38.323 ;
  - for each SRB:
    - if the masterKeyUpdate was not received:
      - configure the PDCP entity for the source PCell with state variables continuation as specified in TS 38.323 ;
    - release the PDCP entity for the target PCell;
    - release the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322 , clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the target PCell;
    - trigger the PDCP entity for the source PCell to perform SDU discard as specified in TS 38.323 ;
    - re-establish the RLC entity for the source PCell;
  - release the physical channel configuration for the target PCell;
  - discard the keys used in target PCell (the K<sub>RRCenc</sub> key, the K<sub>RRCint</sub> key, the K<sub>UPenc</sub> key, the K<sub>UPint</sub> key and the gNB K key), if any;
  - resume suspended SRBs in the source PCell;
  - revert back to the UE configuration used for the DRB or multicast MRB in the source PCell, includes PDCP, RLC states variables, the security configuration and the data stored in transmission and reception buffers in PDCP and RLC entities ;
  - revert back to the UE measurement configuration used in the source PCell;
  - store the handover failure information in VarRLF-Report as described in the clause 5.3.10.5;
  - initiate the failure information procedure as specified in clause 5.7.5 to report DAPS handover failure;
  - revert back to the UE configuration used in the source PCell;
  - if the associated T304 was not initiated upon cell selection performed while timer T311 was running, as defined in clause 5.3.7.3:
    - store the handover failure information in VarRLF-Report as described in the clause 5.3.10.5;
    - initiate the connection re-establishment procedure as specified in clause 5.3.7.

The UE shall:  
1 > else if T304 of a secondary cell group expires:  
2 > if MCG transmission is not suspended:  
3 > release dedicated preambles provided in rach-ConfigDedicated, if configured;  
3 > initiate the SCG failure information procedure as specified in clause 5.7.3 to report SCG reconfiguration with sync failure, upon which the RRC reconfiguration procedure ends;  
3 > if the UE is in NR-DC:  
4 > initiate the connection re-establishment procedure as specified in clause 5.3.7;

The UE shall:  
2 &gt; if MCG transmission is not suspended:  
3 &gt; release dedicated preambles provided in rach-ConfigDedicated, if configured;  
3 &gt; initiate the SCG failure information procedure as specified in clause 5.7.3 to report SCG reconfiguration with sync failure, upon which the RRC reconfiguration procedure ends;  
3 &gt; if the UE is in NR-DC:  
4 &gt; initiate the connection re-establishment procedure as specified in clause 5.3.7;  
3 &gt; else (the UE is in (NG) EN-DC):  
4 &gt; initiate the connection re-establishment procedure as specified in TS 36.331 , clause 5.3.7;

The UE shall:  
2 > if an entry with the matching sl-MeasId exists in the sl-MeasIdList within the VarMeasConfigSL:  
3 > replace the entry with the value received for this sl-MeasId;

If the additionalPmax is present in the same entry of the selected additionalSpectrumEmission within NR-NS-PmaxList, the UE shall:

> apply the additionalPmax;  
> apply the p-Max;

The UE shall:  
1 &gt; if the RRCReconfiguration message includes the sl-L2RemoteUEConfig:  
2 &gt; perform the L2 U2N Remote UE configuration procedure as specified in 5.3.5.16;

For each BH-RLC-ChannelConfig received in the bh-RLC-ChannelToAddModList IE, if the current configuration contains a BH RLC Channel with the received bh-RLC-ChannelID within the same cell group:  
> if reestablishRLC is received:  
>> re-establish the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322;  
> reconfigure the RLC entity or entities in accordance with the received rlc-Config;  
> reconfigure the logical channel in accordance with the received mac-LogicalChannelConfig.

The UE shall:  
1 &gt; for each DRB that is included in the drb-CountMSB-InfoList in the CounterCheck message that is not established:  
2 &gt; include the DRB in the drb-CountInfoList in the CounterCheckResponse message by including the drb-Identity, the count-Uplink and the count-Downlink with the most significant bits set identical to the corresponding values in the drb-CountMSB-InfoList and the least significant bits set to zero;

The UE shall initiate the MeasurementReport procedure:

- after successful AS security activation, when the entry condition applicable for an event-triggered report is fulfilled for one or more applicable cells (or L2 U2N Relay UEs, transmission resource pools, CLI measurement resources) for all measurements after layer 3 filtering taken during timeToTrigger defined for this event within the VarMeasConfig, and:
  - if a first cell triggers the event: include a measurement reporting entry within the VarMeasReportList for this measId and initiate the measurement reporting procedure;
  - if a subsequent cell triggers the event: set the numberOfReportsSent to 0, update the cellsTriggeredList, and initiate the measurement reporting procedure;
  - if the leaving condition is fulfilled and reportOnLeave is set to true: initiate the measurement reporting procedure.

- upon expiry of the periodical reporting timer for this measId: initiate the measurement reporting procedure, as specified in 5.5.5.

- immediately when:
  - RSSI sample values are reported by the physical layer after the first L1 measurement duration (if measRSSI-ReportConfig is configured);
  - a first measurement result is provided from lower layers for ul-DelayValueConfig or ul-ExcessDelayConfig;
  - the quantity to be reported becomes available for the NR SpCell and/or strongest cell (depending on reportAmount);
  - CBR measurement results become available for NR sidelink communication with periodical reporting;
  - a first measurement result is available for cli-Periodical or rxTxPeriodical reporting.

- when the UE acquired SIB1 or detected that the requested NR cell is not transmitting SIB1 (for reportCGI): stop timer T321 and initiate the measurement reporting procedure.

- upon expiry of T321 or T322 for this measId: initiate the measurement reporting procedure.

(All based on clauses [1] and [2] of TS 38.331.)

For each pci-RangeIndex included in the excludedCellsToRemoveList:  
5 > remove the entry with the matching pci-RangeIndex from the excludedCellsToAddModList;  

NOTE 1: For each pci-RangeIndex included in the excludedCellsToRemoveList that concerns overlapping ranges of cells, a cell is removed from the exclude-list of cells only if all PCI ranges containing it are removed.

The UE shall:  
1 > else if inter-RAT cell selection or reselection occurs while T331 is running:  
2 > stop timer T331;  
2 > perform the actions as specified in 5.7.8.3;

The purpose of the Notification message in RRC is **to notify UEs in RRC_IDLE, e.g. about a mobile terminating call** and **to notify UEs about ETWS and/or CMAS**.

From [4] Clause 4.3.1 — Services provided to upper layers:  
> The RRC protocol offers the following services to upper layers:  
> a) Broadcast of common control information;  
> b) Notification of UEs in RRC_IDLE, e.g. about a mobile terminating call;  
> c) Notification of UEs about ETWS and/or CMAS;  
> d) Transfer of dedicated signalling;  
> e) Broadcast of positioning assistance data;  
> f) Transfer of application layer measurement configuration and reporting.

The UE shall perform the following actions upon reception of the RRCReconfigurationFailureSidelink:  
1 > stop timer T400 for the destination, if running;  
1 > continue using the configuration used prior to corresponding RRCReconfigurationSidelink message;  
1 > if UE is in RRC_CONNECTED:  
2 > perform the sidelink UE information for NR sidelink communication procedure, as specified in 5.8.3.3 or clause 5.10.15 in TS 36.331.

If the RRCReconfiguration includes the scg-State, the UE shall:

- perform SCG deactivation as specified in 5.3.5.13b;  
- perform SCG activation as specified in 5.3.5.13a.

When the RRCReconfiguration includes daps-SourceRelease, for each DAPS bearer:

- release the RLC entity or entities as specified in TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the source SpCell;
- reconfigure the PDCP entity to release DAPS as specified in TS 38.323.

For each SRB, when the RRCReconfiguration includes daps-SourceRelease:

- release the PDCP entity for the source SpCell;  
- release the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322, clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the source SpCell.

The UE shall:  
1 &gt; else if this procedure was initiated due to reception of the sk-Counter (UE is in NE-DC, or NR-DC, or is configured with SN terminated bearer(s)):  
2 &gt; derive or update the secondary key (S-K or S-KeNB) based on the KgNB key and using the received sk-Counter value, as specified in TS 33.501 ;  
2 &gt; derive the K and K keys as specified in TS 33.501 using the ciphering algorithms RRCenc UPenc indicated in the RadioBearerConfig associated with the secondary key (S-K or S-KeNB) as indicated by gNB keyToUse;  
2 &gt; derive the K and K keys as specified in TS 33.501 using the integrity protection RRCint UPint algorithms indicated in the RadioBearerConfig associated with the secondary key (S-K or S-KeNB) as gNB indicated by keyToUse;

The UE shall:  
1 &gt; consider inter-RAT mobility as initiated towards UTRA-FDD;  
1 &gt; forward the nas-SecurityParamFromNR to the upper layers, if included;  
1 &gt; access the target cell indicated in the inter-RAT message in accordance with the specifications of the target RAT.
